  "historical_output_text": " Here's how one could help answer such an everyday forum issue:\n\nQ) The toilet keeps cavititing - I press and hold on but the flush still won ' t finish . Help ?\n\nWhen the water isn t flushing out and stopping after you hit 'start', that often indicates a partial or completely blocked vent in or above your drain pipes. When this air passage becomes clogs or restricted the air pressure balance that allows normal flushing breaks and you just get slow, partial fills without proper drainage happening - it feels \"cavitate\" but the toilet itself isn' working as normal should.\n\nHere’s the quick test and solution:\n\nTry using an old, thin hanger. Make 2 bends at 7 inch angles, then bend another section to create an \"armature hook.\" This acts just right in most 3-inch pipe drain openings - the",
